# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Two rules govern this file and they pull in opposite directions, so both are written out:
#
#   1. Nothing secret. `.env`, `.env.local` and every `.env.*.local` hold SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY,
#      which bypasses every RLS policy. A build context is readable by every stage of the
#      build and, for anything a stage COPYs, by anyone who can pull the image. The secret
#      reaches the running system as a container environment variable at run time and by no
#      other route — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "Environment variables".
#
#   2. Nothing missing. vite.config.js imports scripts/lib/*.mjs, and src/lib/scenes.js
#      imports content/darshan.json — both are build inputs that do not look like build
#      inputs. Excluding a directory here fails at `npm run build` inside the image, which is
#      a slow way to find out. Add to this list only after checking nothing imports it.

# ── dependencies and build output: rebuilt inside the image, never copied in ──
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
dev-dist

# ── secrets, in every spelling .gitignore already knows about ──
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.production

# ── version control and CI ──
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude

# ── the artwork masters. 549 MB of PNG that nothing in the build reads: દર્શન images are
#    fetched from Google's CDN by absolute URL at run time (docs/IMAGE_CONTRACT.md).
assets
originals-archive

# ── database migrations and their test harness. Applied with scripts/db.mjs against
#    Supabase, never from a container.
supabase

# ── prose, and the one stray file under dev/ ──
*.md
docs
dev

# ── this deployment's own artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# FOUR FILES UNDER deploy/ ARE BUILD INPUTS and must not be excluded:
#   deploy/nginx-main.conf   replaces /etc/nginx/nginx.conf so the server can run non-root
#   deploy/nginx.conf        the site rules
#   deploy/api-proxy.inc     what the three proxied locations share
#   deploy/entrypoint.sh     starts both processes; the image does not run without it
#
# So `deploy/*.sh` is NOT excluded wholesale — entrypoint.sh lives there. The host-side scripts
# are named one by one instead. Excluding entrypoint.sh produces a build that succeeds and an
# image that cannot start, which is a slow way to find out.
compose.yaml
compose.production.yaml
deploy/deploy.sh
deploy/push-dockerhub.sh
deploy/rollback.sh
deploy/health-check.sh
deploy/vps-setup.sh
deploy/Caddyfile
deploy/.env.production.example

# ── local noise ──
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
